			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract Configuration DTOs and service into file-per-struct modules\n\nDecompose the new Configuration RPC module to align with the project-wide PascalCase file-per-struct convention. Create dedicated `ConfigurationScope.rs`, `ConfigurationService.rs`, and `ConfigurationUpdate.rs` files within `Source/RPC/Configuration`.\n\nThe `ConfigurationScope` enum defines Global, Workspace, and Folder scopes. `ConfigurationUpdate` acts as the DTO carrying key, value, and scope for configuration changes. `ConfigurationService` implements a placeholder in-memory key-value store using `HashMap<String, Value>` with `get` and `set` methods. All files define their core types as `Struct` or `Enum` to satisfy Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro symbol resolution requirements, mirroring the architectural pattern established in recent Echo, Telemetry, Workspace, and Vine refactors.",
			"SHA": "118c95c7742e8f7cce344f7cb801d3f8d3d245f4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
